 src=\"/media/cfd9c3df7083f6317dd9149dbdb2cee852972bbb.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"single | Marks +2 / -0.66"},{"qnum":5,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"/media/8981fd08aee8cafd81461225f68c570c7549e66d.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>\n<div><span>Numerical answer type</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"1.1","high":"1.12"},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/d5ed2bae27164d40e9a930be71cd36c3a0aa72e1.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/3ae6afb4239b91bd7f2cffeb583ce53f49d2d131.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"numerical | Marks +2"},{"qnum":6,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"/media/a053b35a11c61ceba44c9eaa1122994330ef51e8.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/f1c08210dbf421230be9fc8d2c928fde0b5c267b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/96d483e44a42a8d9fb1177d65dfcab2b5dea9180.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/d345b60a7aec44a73737ecec1ea3e62a5ff500fa.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/b1a70540154c0950afc0cb05941fb198ebbe785b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/a1c5d9f17c9992e7668be802da5dd4de38d97b25.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"single | Marks +1 / -0.33"},{"qnum":7,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>Nyquist plots of two functions <em>G</em><sub>1</sub>(<em>s</em>) and <em>G</em><sub>2</sub>(<em>s</em>) are shown in figure below,</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/5b1abb63feee26969386921afdbb396afa06b0f9.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>Nyquist plot of the product of <em>G</em><sub>1</sub>(<em>s</em>) and <em>G</em><sub>2</sub>(<em>s</em>) is</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/094f5a8ea4a4109252